 * 3. Create a valid notification event using required fields only (recipient_member_id, event_type, status)
 * 4. Validate the notification record is returned with correct fields (including id, timestamps)
 * 5. Attempt to create notifications with missing required properties (recipient_member_id, event_type, status)
 * 6. Attempt to create notifications with invalid fields (empty event_type or status)
 * 7. Attempt to create a notification with a non-existent recipient_member_id (should fail by business logic)
 *
 * All negative cases must result in validation or business rule error responses. No external data or pre-existing members are assumed except admin registration.
