 * 2. Login as Member A and create a new board post
 * 3. Post one comment as Member A, and another as Member B
 * 4. (a) As Member A, update own comment body within allowed edit window: expect update to succeed, check body and updated_at metadata
 * 5. (b) Simulate passing edit window (by manually updating 'created_at' if possible via setup) and attempt edit: expect error (if not feasible, note limitation)
 * 6. (c) As Member B, attempt to update Member A's comment: expect error (permission denied)
 * 7. (d) Delete Member A's comment, then attempt to update it: expect error (cannot edit deleted)
 * 8. (e) [FLAGGING/LOCKING test] For flagged: edit as Member A, expect error (skip if flag cannot be set). For locked: not possible unless lock property exists.
